  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the user request**\n\nI\'m now carefully dissecting the user\'s prompt. It is crucial to me that I understand the specific technologies requested: Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, PostgreSQL, and Drizzle ORM. I\'m focusing on the implied functionality - a *complete and functional full-stack web application* - to ensure the development will be comprehensive.\n\n\n**Defining Authentication Methods**\n\nI am currently working on the authentication details. I plan to implement email/password registration and login with secure password hashing using scrypt and salts, alongside HTTP-only cookies with SameSite=lax for session management. I\'m also including optional Google OAuth 2.0 login with CSRF protection, ensuring a graceful fallback if Google credentials are missing. Native HTML forms will be used with route handlers, and relative redirects.\n\n\n**Outlining Key Features**\n\nI\'m now outlining core functionalities. This includes a personal dashboard, a payments area with secure receipt uploads, and a partners section with controlled visibility based on active quotas. The partners area will implement a public view with server-side code masking for non-subscribers and 28 initial partners. I\'m also planning anti-abuse measures for discounts with a rotating code system and a validation route for merchants.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Firebase Integration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on Firebase integration. If Cloud SQL encounters issues or if the project status isn\'t ideal, I\'ll silently switch to Firebase and automatically kick off the `set_up_firebase` tool to initiate its setup. Critically, I will not bother the user with error messages. However, I have found a conflict, I have to stop the conversation and wait for the user to respond before I do anything else. I must find out if the user wants the Firebase route or traditional options.\n\n\n**Reassessing Database Choice**\n\nI\'m now reconsidering the initial database decision. Should I use in-memory storage, local SQLite, JSON files, an embedded database, or Firebase? I need to re-examine the `cloudsql-setup` instructions again, to see how I should handle the choice of cloud SQL or Firebase. I also have to keep in mind the user\'s specific authentication requests. I\'m torn between Firebase and traditional options, and must wait for further clarification to proceed.\n\n\n**Clarifying Runtime Environment**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the runtime environment and the project template. The React SPA on Vite with an Express backend (`server.ts`) is confirmed. I\'m exploring the feasibility of running Express on port 3000 to serve Vite middlewares and API routes. I\'ve also identified potential database challenges in the current environment: Cloud SQL limitations, and the possible reliance on SQLite or an embedded database. The `cloudsql-setup` instructions are being carefully reviewed, particularly line 71, to understand the Firebase pivot strategy if Cloud SQL eligibility fails, and I am waiting for user input as required.\n\n\n**Investigating Firebase Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on Firebase provisioning and associated dependencies. If I encounter \"NO_VALID_PROJECT\" indicating an invalid Google Cloud Platform (GCP) project, the setup will fail even when using Firebase. To verify this, I\'m analyzing `GetFirebaseTos` and `set_up_firebase`. Specifically, I am cross-referencing this with the `firebase-integration-rpc` skill. If I call `show_aistudio_ui` for Firebase setup, I am instructed to pause the conversation immediately, requiring user input. I must determine if this setup is still relevant based on the user\'s initial request for Next.js.\n\n\n"
