  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Frontend Design**\n\nI\'m now starting on the React client application, using Tailwind CSS for styling. I\'ve begun reviewing the frontend requirements. Currently, my focus is on the navigation bar, specifically the inclusion of the LPCS logo, subtitle, and associated links.\n\n\n**Defining Navigation Structure**\n\nI\'ve outlined the core routes for the application: Home, Partners & Discounts, Dashboard, Payments & Dues, Profile, Validate Discount (for merchants), and Backoffice (for admins). I\'m also planning the right-side navigation elements: a quota status badge, user information, and login/logout button. Now, I am structuring the homepage, building a dynamic hero section based on the database, and focusing on key metrics like total savings and return on investment.\n\n\n**Structuring Homepage Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the homepage\'s highlights. I\'m incorporating a \"Paga a quota\" badge for users with significant savings (>=35\342\202\254), and developing an overview of activity areas with links. I\'m also structuring a quotas comparison, and a final CTA merging solidarity, social impact, and benefits. Finally, I\'m working on the partner page, ensuring a public catalog of all partners with discount access restricted to quota holders, including details on card display and appropriate CTA\'s.\n\n\n**Developing Partner Filters**\n\nI\'m now detailing the partner page filters. I\'m focusing on a family of activities with count pills, district and city selectors, and benefit type filters (Coupon, Code, Voucher). There\'s also a free search input for comprehensive searches. I\'m including a results counter and a clear filters button, along with an empty state. I\'m also planning the design for the anti-abuse rotating code modal. I\'m using an HMAC-SHA256 derived 6-digit code, changing every 30 seconds, dynamic countdown progress bar, and a watermark repeating the associate\'s member number and timestamp across the background.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the dashboard. I\'m focusing on a prominent quota validity panel with a traffic light system indicating validity status, along with the \"valid until\" date, days remaining, and a progress bar. I\'m also including a quick quota payment/renewal form, a recent payments table, and quick links to partners and receipts.\n\n\n**Refining Receipt Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the receipt archive. I\'m building an upload form for PDF, PNG, JPG, and WEBP files (up to 5MB), and it will include fields for a note and quota association. I\'m also creating a list to display uploaded receipts, providing view/download and delete functionalities. I am going to make each entry clickable, linking to an API endpoint.\n\n\n**Constructing Admin Backoffice**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on the admin backoffice area. I\'m verifying access control using a double-check to ensure that only \"admin@lpcs.pt\" with `is_admin = true` can access it. I\'m also planning the summary metrics display, including total associates, revenue, and redemptions. I\'m also moving on to the associates management section and the partner management tools. I\'m starting by adding the foundation for the real-time audit logs viewer.\n\n\n**Finalizing UI Pages**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the user interface, incorporating the footer with legal information and contact details. I\'ve built the super-secure, rotating TOTP code modal with auto-close, blur, and watermark. The home and partners pages are now populated with dynamic content and member-specific access controls. I\'ve also implemented the merchant verification page, personal dashboard, payments, profile editor, and login/registration pages. The admin backoffice is complete.\n\n\n"
