  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Foundation**\n\nI\'m solidifying the core architecture. I\'m focusing on the database and API. My priority is establishing the `partner_inquiries` table within the database, which will be the central hub for collecting corporate partnership proposals. I\'m thinking through its structure: `company_name`, `nif`, `contact_name`, and `email`, are crucial for initial data collection.\n\n\n**Expanding the Inquiry System**\n\nI\'m now integrating phone, address details, proposed benefit, and website fields into the `partner_inquiries` table. I\'m also planning the `POST /api/partners/inquiry` endpoint, ensuring it validates submissions and logs audits. This public endpoint will collect the necessary corporate partnership data. Following that, I\'ll build the admin interfaces for reviewing and updating the status of the inquiries at `/admin` (requiring admin auth).\n\n\n\n**Visualizing Page Structure**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the page\'s visual layout. My focus is the initial \"hero\" section, particularly the placement and prominence of calls to action. I want to highlight the \"Login para S\303\263cios\" functionality and also the \"Quero Fazer Parceria\" button, right in the Hero CTA row. I\'m exploring a 12-column grid to achieve this, making sure the key elements are immediately visible upon landing. I\'m considering cards or distinct sections for the login portal, and membership information, depending on user state.\n\n\n**Showcasing Partnership Benefits**\n\nI\'m now outlining a dedicated section, accessible from the homepage and `/parceria`, that highlights the benefits of partnering with LPCS. I\'m focusing on \"Responsabilidade Social\", \"Benef\303\255cios Fiscais\" via the \"Estatuto do Mecenato\", and enhanced \"Visibilidade & Novos Clientes\". It will also include a \"Zero\" section about the association. This is intended to be a compelling showcase for potential corporate partners.\n\n\n**Refining Benefits Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed partnership benefits. I\'m focusing on \"Custos de Ades\303\243o\" which is free, and security which will use HMAC-SHA256 for validation. I\'m also ensuring flexibility with options like promotional coupons, discount codes, and vouchers. Moreover, I\'m incorporating employee engagement through health initiatives as part of the offering. I\'m also embedding the \"Quero Fazer Parceria\" form for direct proposals.\n\n\n"
