  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Cookie Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a specific scenario: what happens when a user\'s browser, like Chrome Incognito or Safari, blocks `SameSite=None; Secure` third-party cookies within the AI Studio preview iframe. I\'m trying to determine the implications of this cookie blockage in that context.\n\n\n**Analyzing Login Issues**\n\nI\'m now investigating a user\'s reported login problem. It seems their browser, likely in a private browsing mode, isn\'t persisting any cookies within the AI Studio iframe. My current hypothesis is that the iframe is missing a token, which creates a login issue. I\'m focusing on why a user cannot log in and how to best address this. I\'m checking if the original setup matches the original prompt, which used `httpOnly, SameSite=lax` cookies.\n\n\n**Addressing Login Loops**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial bug: I found that `onRefreshUser()` calls, in both `LoginPage.tsx` and `HomePage.tsx`, were not awaited. This meant the application immediately navigated to the dashboard, but since the user data wasn\'t updated yet, it immediately bounced back to the login page, creating a loop. This happened across all environments, including `localhost`. My focus has shifted to implementing the fix to resolve this login loop, by awaiting the data. I\'m also confirming the fix with cross-site `sameSite: none` calls.\n\n\n"
