  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Auto-Close Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the auto-close functionality within `CodeModal.tsx`. I\'ve pinpointed the `autoCloseRemaining` state variable and its initial value, directly linked to the 2-minute auto-close timer. Furthermore, I am now understanding how this remaining time is displayed in the user interface.\n\n\n**Adjusting Auto-Close Duration**\n\nI\'ve been working on extending the 6-digit code\'s availability. Updating `autoCloseRemaining` in `CodeModal.tsx` to 180 seconds ensures the code stays visible for the desired 3 minutes, and I\'m considering clear UI formatting for time display. I\'m also now considering the server-side code\'s 15-minute validity, to determine if the user\'s focus is just on the UI, the API, or both aspects of availability.\n\n\n**Clarifying Code Availability**\n\nI\'m now diving into the interplay of different timings. In `totp.ts`, the code rotates every 30 seconds. The modal previously auto-closed after 2 minutes, and the redemption was valid for 15 minutes. The user wants a 3-minute display. I\'m confirming that extending the UI display to 3 minutes won\'t conflict with the 15-minute server-side validity. This means the rotating codes are available for the entirety of the intended display time.\n\n\n"
