  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Qualities**\n\nI\'m struck by the genuine warmth and authentic editorial quality of those images. They perfectly capture the spirit of Lisbon and Portugal, with a cohesive tone. We\'re on the right track! The provided paths confirm they\'ll integrate nicely: `/src/assets/images/hero_lpcs_community_1794510456196.jpg` and `/src/assets/images/hero_lpcs_community_1794510456201.jpg`. Now I\'m preparing the integration plan.\n\n\n**Confirming Vite Asset Handling**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specific Vite asset handling. I need to verify that image paths resolve correctly via static ES imports, or through the `public/` folder, or both, as per the established pattern. The `frontend-design` notes suggest direct imports within client-side components are the safest approach in Vite for the production build. I\'m also planning to add an `onError` state fallback to image slots.\n\n\n**Planning Design Cohesion**\n\nI\'m developing a meticulous plan to elevate the visual experience in Phase 2, focusing on design cohesion and trustworthiness. I\'ve begun with `/index.html` and `/src/index.css`, integrating Google Fonts for a refined typographic hierarchy: Fraunces, Plus Jakarta Sans, and JetBrains Mono. I\'m setting a body background of `#FAF8F5` with a deep ink color of `#141619`, and establishing crisp typography defaults, smooth transitions, and accessibility considerations. I am also planning the `/src/components/Header.tsx` file now.\n\n\n**Designing Navigation and Footer**\n\nI\'m now detailing the navigation and footer components. I\'m prioritizing a clean, efficient aesthetic. I\'m focusing on single-line links for Zone 2, and concise logged-out/logged-in states for Zone 3 in the header. For the footer, I\'m designing a refined, dark, and institutional layout with real IPSS details and a focus on clean typography, and hairline dividers, with no pulsing elements. I also need to focus on `/src/components/Footer.tsx`.\n\n\n**Crafting Hero Section**\n\nI am now focusing on `/src/pages/HomePage.tsx`, particularly the hero section. I\'m aiming for an asymmetric, museum-grade layout on a `max-w-7xl` desktop presence. The left column will feature an institutional kicker, a balanced display headline highlighting savings, a clear lead paragraph, and both primary and secondary CTAs. The right column will combine the community photograph with a refined login or active member card. Below this, I plan a full-width operational & impact strip with three editorial stat columns.\n\n\n**Structuring Content Display**\n\nI\'m now detailing a deep charcoal architectural section with an asymmetric, two-column value ledger that compares annual contributions to average benefits, with fine hairline separation. I am designing a four-column catalog grid with single-elevation cards that highlight member benefits with tabular numbers and adjacent editorial strips with lifestyle photography. I\'m also preparing a directory grid for activity areas, and a dedicated partnership section for companies.\n\n\n**Developing Partnership Page**\n\nI\'m now detailing `/src/pages/PartnersPage.tsx`. I am focusing on a clean institutional catalog header with a CTA for non-members. I am also working on a refined search & filter bar, with segmented area filter buttons, cascading Distrito/Localidade/Tipo selects, and a tabular result count. I\'m prioritizing elevated Partner Cards with a clean visual design.\n\n\n**Refining Partner Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the Partner Cards within `/src/pages/PartnersPage.tsx`. I\'m detailing clean, unboxed metadata headers, a strong partner title, a crisp discount highlight band, and single clear action footers. For the Partner corporate alliance page, I\'m integrating a full-width editorial marquee with a measured contrast scrim. I\'m also preparing corporate advantages, a merchant validation explainer, and a corporate proposal form for the page.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing architectural cards with `tabular-nums` throughout the design. I\'ve designed a refined digital member card and a traffic-light quota panel in the dashboard, with no hue-only elements or pulsing. The payment plan and method selectors are designed with `MB WAY`, `Multibanco`, and `Cart\303\243o`, along with compact high-density data tables, with crisp `border-b border-stone-100` rows. I am also working on the `/perfil` form with a live NIF indicator.\n\n\n"
