    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Configurations**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring the project cleanly fulfills every part of the user\'s request, specifically with the Helvetica and its variations in `index.html` and `src/index.css`. I\'ve removed the specified fonts from Google Fonts in `index.html` and started configuring these components.\n\n\n**Refining Font Usage**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on fine-tuning Helvetica\'s implementation across the codebase. I\'m focusing on `--font-sans` and `--font-display`, ensuring `Helvetica Neue`, Helvetica, Arial, and sans-serif are prioritized and crisp across different OSes and environments, with `JetBrains Mono` for monospace elements. The idea is to use Helvetica variations for different text elements: bold variations for headlines, light or regular for body copy, medium or semi-bold for navigation, and bold for key metrics.\n\n\n**Implementing Font Variations**\n\nI\'m now implementing the deliberate Helvetica typographic variations in the UI, assigning weights to specific elements: bold for headlines, light for subtitles, normal for body copy, and medium/semibold for labels and navigation. This involves adjusting the font-weight and letter-spacing values to achieve the desired effect. Furthermore, I\'m working to integrate the logo assets seamlessly.\n\n\n**Integrating Logo Asset**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided logo asset, ensuring it renders crisply. The image has significant white padding, which I\'ll address by using `object-contain` or placing it in a white container, possibly with subtle cropping. I\'ll verify the dimensions and bounding box. I plan to use the image with `h-12 w-auto object-contain` on a white background in the header, and also in white badges/cards within dark sections. In the header, I\'ll use a white background with the logo `<img src=\"/assets/aistudio/logo_LPCS_f0a028f9.jpg\" alt=\"Liga Portuguesa Contra a SIDA\" className=\"h-12 w-auto object-contain\" />`.\n\n\n**Incorporating Identification Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the LPCS identification data. I plan to feature the official logo prominently in `Footer.tsx` alongside the full legal identification block. I\'m also considering adding a clean identification strip or band, perhaps within the Hero or About sections, in `HomePage.tsx` to provide immediate visibility of the official LPCS identity. This should ensure the necessary details are present and accessible.\n\n\n"
